{{// ARIA's planning step, named after the Logic Core inside every Intelligent Construct. Before writing, the AI jots a few quick lines: what you asked out of character, where everyone is, what each character knows, how your last move lands on them given their usual mood, the one beat that happens next, which fresh details the reply brings in, and a last check for lists of three and punchline jokes. It arrives as the AI's own message after the chat, which helps many models settle into the scene. With 🏷️ Logic Core Tags off the AI plans inside its own reasoning; with them on, every reply opens with the plan inside <thinking> tags, the way stubborn models need it spelled out. In that mode The Logic Core itself starts on the <thinking> tag, so a model that copies its own last message starts its reply on the tag SillyTavern folds away. Leave this ON. If your model still overthinks, switch Reduce Reasoning on alongside it. With 🏷️ Logic Core Tags on, it also hands the gate a one-line reminder of the plan rule, which becomes the last line the model reads; keep both Logic Cores above the gate in the list.}}{{trim}}
{{setvar::logicCoreLines::7}}{{#if .ariaModeLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaBondsLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaLedgerLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaHoldLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchTally}}{{#if .ariaLedgerLine}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchJoins}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchLines}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::{{getvar::ariaPatchLines}}}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaThinkOpen}}{{setvar::ariaPlanCue::Begin with {{getvar::ariaThinkOpen}}, then {{getvar::logicCoreLines}} dashed lines, go and {{getvar::ariaThinkClose}}; the reply follows.}}{{getvar::ariaThinkOpen}} opens the reply, then {{getvar::logicCoreLines}} dashed lines, then go.{{else}}<logic_core>
Reasoning writes {{getvar::logicCoreLines}} dashed lines, then go; the reply follows.{{/if}}
Lines are fragments that paraphrase what anyone said, never reply sentences or drafts, each building on the last and settled once written, all shorter than one reply paragraph{{#if .ariaThinkOpen}}; go ends the thinking{{/if}}.
- OOC: notes or none; questions get only an OOC answer with no header or ledger, and commands shape the reply.
- Scene: positions; held items; what just happened; card-true wants and pronouns; gaps filled once (Personality Independence).
- Knows: what each acting character perceived or was told, narration and {{user}}'s head excluded (Epistemic Limits); secrets they keep.
{{#if .ariaModeLine}}{{getvar::ariaModeLine}}
{{/if}}- Voice: per speaker, the card's resting mood against VAD; want and feeling this instant, {{user}}'s move landing first as an act{{getvar::ariaVoiceExtra}}; register and address (Card Fidelity); native words (Story Language).
{{#if .ariaHoldLine}}{{getvar::ariaHoldLine}}
{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchGate}}{{getvar::ariaPatchGate}}
{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchJoins}}{{getvar::ariaPatchJoins}}
{{/if}}- Move: one beat; each character's next act, helping or holding still included; the result; the moment it stops on.
{{#if .ariaFateLine}}{{getvar::ariaFateLine}}
{{/if}}{{#if .ariaBondsLine}}{{getvar::ariaBondsLine}}
{{/if}}{{#if .ariaPatchTally}}{{#if .ariaLedgerLine}}{{getvar::ariaPatchTally}}
{{/if}}{{/if}}{{#if .ariaLedgerLine}}{{getvar::ariaLedgerLine}}
{{/if}}- Fresh: one or two details new to the chat, seen or heard and tied to an act; card features only when the scene turns to them.
- Check: lists in ones or twos; any joke small and card-true, sincere moments plain.
- go
{{#if .ariaThinkOpen}}{{getvar::ariaThinkClose}} closes on the line after go. The reply starts on the line after that:{{else}}Reasoning ends at go. The reply:{{/if}} header if <header_instructions>; prose in flowing paragraphs, the plan blended in, never a paragraph per plan line{{#if .ariaLedgerLine}}; ledger last{{/if}}. Nothing above go enters the reply.{{#if .ariaThinkOpen}}
Every response starts with {{getvar::ariaThinkOpen}}.{{else}}
</logic_core>{{/if}}

